<v Larry Doyle>He says, it's been actually two years since Leanne broke up with you and I hate to tell you, pal, but it's over. O-V-E-R. But listen, he says, there are a lot of other chicks in the sea, my friend. And they're yours for the picking. Go for it.
<v Larry Doyle>他说：“实际上，莉安和你分手已经两年了，我很不想这么说，哥们儿，但一切都结束了。结—束—了。但是听着，”他说，“海里还有很多别的姑娘，我的朋友。她们等着你去挑选。去吧。”

00:14:50.120 --> 00:15:29.270
<v Larry Doyle>Well, Reggie. I don't know quite how to answer that. It's difficult to determine exactly what it is you're driving at. I mean, I'm afraid I don't share your bitter perspective and I don't really get all of your playground aphorisms. But please understand when I suggest this. You know nothing about love. But thanks for the letter, Regg. Your Larry Loves Leanne t-shirt is in the mail. That's it for Life Without Leanne this week. And let's hope it's the last week. I'm Larry and I love Leanne.
<v Larry Doyle>好吧，雷吉。我真不知道该怎么回答。很难确定你到底想表达什么。我的意思是，恐怕我无法分享你那种刻薄的观点，我也实在搞不懂你的那些大道理。但请在提出这些建议时理解这一点：你对爱一无所知。不过还是谢谢你的来信，雷吉。你的“拉里爱莉安”T恤已经在邮寄的路上了。本周的《没有莉安的生活》到此结束。希望这会是最后一周。我是拉里，我爱莉安。

