00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:55.500
<v Beau O'reilly>Eddie Hickock Collins taught high school English in Baldwin, Long Island. Remedial readers whose attention spans kept them far away from Herman Melville or Nathaniel Hawthorne. Holden Caulfield in Catcher in The Rye , those seemed just right to Eddie, despite the fact that Catcher in The Rye was on the banned bookshelf of the school library.
<v Beau O'reilly>埃迪·希科克·柯林斯在长岛鲍德温教高中英语。那些阅读困难的学生注意力范围远不及赫尔曼·梅尔维尔或纳撒尼尔·霍桑。在《麦田里的守望者》中，霍尔顿·考菲尔德对埃迪来说似乎恰到好处，尽管事实上《麦田里的守望者》当时在学校图书馆的禁书架上。

00:16:55.500 --> 00:17:14.850
<v Beau O'reilly>The library didn't like the use of the F word on page 201 of Catcher in The Rye . But page 201 was Eddie Collins' favorite page. And he figured his remedial readers would love it too. His young hooligans who all wanted and needed to get naked and needed page 201 thought Eddie.
<v Beau O'reilly>图书馆不喜欢《麦田里的守望者》第201页上使用F开头的词。但第201页是埃迪·柯林斯最喜欢的一页。他觉得他的差生们也会喜欢它的。他那些渴望也需要变得赤裸、并且需要第201页的少年捣蛋鬼们，埃迪心想。

00:17:14.850 --> 00:17:29.100
<v Beau O'reilly>The school soon gave notice though. Under no circumstances was he to teach that dirty Catcher in The Rye. The F word, beloved page 201. They were deemed questionable and inappropriate.
<v Beau O'reilly>但学校很快就发出了通知。无论如何，他都不准教那本肮脏的《麦田里的守望者》。那个F开头的词，心爱的第201页。它们被认为是有问题的和不恰当的。

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:51.700
<v Beau O'reilly>Eddie began reading the book aloud to his remedial class that day. And the remedial readers all took notice. They nodded and they grunted at all the good parts. And running their long, adolescent fingers over and over through their greasy pompadours as good, old Holden Caulfield rolled along. And cheering and chanting out the F word when Eddie tore into page 201.
<v Beau O'reilly>埃迪那天开始向他的差生班朗读这本书。那些学生全都注意听了。他们对所有精彩的部分点头赞许、咕哝着回应。当老霍尔顿·考菲尔德的故事推进时，他们用长长的、青春期的手指一遍又一遍地梳理着自己油腻的蓬巴杜发型。而当埃迪撕开第201页读到那个词时，他们欢呼雀跃，齐声高喊。

00:17:51.700 --> 00:18:02.770
<v Beau O'reilly>Edward Hickock Collins was fired from teaching high school English in Baldwin, Long Island. And he spent the rest of that year pacing in front of the fireplace at his mother's house.
<v Beau O'reilly>爱德华·希科克·柯林斯被长岛鲍德温的高中解聘了。那一年的余下时间，他都在他母亲家的壁炉前踱步。

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:39.890
<v Beau O'reilly>It was a cold winter, but Eddie was already heated up from his recent battle with censorship, so Eddie pulled off more and more of his clothes. His shirt, his shoes, his pants. And he flung them in all directions. Eddie built up the fire and he sweated aloud. If he couldn't teach the F word, how could he live free? That he demanded of himself. The F word, the sex act. That had to be naked and lovely. That felt right and right felt natural. And why hide that, Eddie thought. And that's when he first thought it. He would never dress again.
<v Beau O'reilly>那是一个寒冷的冬天，但埃迪因最近那场反审查制度的战斗而变得亢奋，于是埃迪脱掉了越来越多的衣服。他的衬衫、鞋子、裤子。他把它们向各个方向扔去。埃迪生起了火，大声喘着气。如果他不能教授那个词，他还怎么能活得自由？他对自己发出质问。那个词，性行为。那必须是赤裸而可爱的。那感觉是对的，而正确的感觉是自然的。埃迪心想，为什么要隐藏这些呢？就在那时，他有了第一个想法。他再也不会穿衣服了。

00:18:39.890 --> 00:19:17.010
<v Beau O'reilly>You know how an idea catches and grabs a hold of you? Maybe you've had that. An idea that speaks to your most private imaginings and your deepest hurt feelings, your most secret strange joys. And that idea says, here I am. Change everything because I'm here. I'm perfect. I'm enlightened by sexuality. I'm the new laughing cure for cancer. I am my body and shape and in perfect yoga pose. And these ideas fuel so crucial that the access of your world turns to embrace them.
<v Beau O'reilly>你知道一个想法是如何捕捉并抓住你的吗？也许你也有过这样的经历。一个触动你最私密的幻想、最深沉受伤的情感、最隐秘奇异的快乐的想法。那个想法说：“我就在这里。改变一切吧，因为我在这里。我是完美的。我被性启蒙。我是癌症的新型幽默疗法。我是我的身体，我的形态，我的完美瑜伽姿势。”这些想法如此至关重要，以至于你世界的轴心都随之转动以拥抱它们。

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:31.620
<v Beau O'reilly>Eddie's idea felt like that. And Eddie's idea was naked and it was obvious. It was without guilt or second thought. Nudity. Nudity now.
<v Beau O'reilly>埃迪的想法就是这种感觉。而埃迪的想法是赤裸的，显而易见的。它没有负罪感，也没有第二种想法。裸体。现在就裸体。

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:42.350
<v Beau O'reilly>Eddie ran naked all the way to the high school. It was his first nude run. His body was flapping like a ship that has come free of its moorings and is now spinning and reckless in the surf.
<v Beau O'reilly>埃迪赤身裸体一路跑向高中。这是他第一次裸奔。他的身体像一艘脱离了系泊的船，在浪潮中疯狂地旋转，毫无拘束。

00:19:42.350 --> 00:20:01.160
<v Beau O'reilly>And at the high school, all his former students, the remedial readers, they were playing manic playground basketball. And Eddie happily ran out on the court. He wanted to dunk a few in the glorious springtime. Dunk a few and then tell the smart guys of his new vision of freedom.
<v Beau O'reilly>在高中，他以前所有的学生，那些差生，正在疯狂地玩着操场篮球。埃迪快乐地冲上球场。他想在辉煌的春日里扣上几个篮。扣上几个篮，然后告诉这些“聪明人”他那关于自由的新愿景。

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:16.820
<v Beau O'reilly>And Eddie yelled in his joy as he hit the court, but his remedial readers weren't glad to see him. They turned away, laughing, embarrassed by Eddie's nakedness. And they refused to pass him the ball.
<v Beau O'reilly>埃迪满心欢喜地大喊着跑上球场，但那些差生看到他并不高兴。他们转过身去，嘲笑着，为埃迪的裸体感到尴尬。他们拒绝传球给他。

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:35.270
<v Beau O'reilly>And when Eddie persisted, he leaped at each one of the boys in turn. One of them grabbed the ball and smacked it into Eddie's face hard. So hard the ball flip stung and bled and Eddie's eyes filled with tears.
<v Beau O'reilly>当埃迪坚持时，他依次扑向每一个男孩。其中一个抢过球，重重地砸在埃迪脸上。那球砸得非常疼，他流血了，埃迪的眼里噙满了泪水。

00:20:35.270 --> 00:20:45.650
<v Beau O'reilly>Eddie was lost then. The remedial readers surrounded and hounded him. Oh, they flicked popsicle sticks and clouds of dirt at his exposed penis and his poor back side.
<v Beau O'reilly>埃迪在那一刻迷失了。那些学生包围并驱赶他。哦，他们弹着冰棍棒，将尘土扬向他暴露的生殖器和他可怜的背部。

00:20:45.650 --> 00:21:19.580
<v Beau O'reilly>And Eddie slammed the door of his mother's house. He was crying and he was shaking. And all the remedial readers, they gathered in a pack outside. They were flushed and they talked themselves into a deeper hatred. And one of them grabbed a brick and threw it through Eddie's mother's picture window and shattered it. And then there was such a roar of rage and hurt and it just ripped through Eddie's brain and he grabbed the same brick and he threw it back through the same window. The remaining glass just flying. And then, Eddie jumped through the now open window, falling and gashing his poor hands and his poor feet.
<v Beau O'reilly>埃迪砰地一声关上母亲家的门。他哭着，颤抖着。而所有那些差生，他们在外面聚集成群。他们满脸通红，鼓动自己产生更深的仇恨。其中一个抓起一块砖头，砸向埃迪母亲的画窗，玻璃碎了。接着，一阵愤怒和伤害的咆哮穿过了埃迪的大脑，他抓起同一块砖头，又把它扔回了同一个窗户。剩下的玻璃随之飞溅。然后，埃迪跳过了现在洞开的窗户，重重摔倒，划伤了他可怜的手脚。

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:39.030
<v Beau O'reilly>The remedial readers running in all directions. Eddie landing on a lawn of glass. And when he looked up in the sky, written in huge letters of flaming black and red six feet high were the words, "Why? Don't ask why. Live."
<v Beau O'reilly>差生们四散奔逃。埃迪跌落在满是玻璃的草坪上。当他抬头望向天空时，上面用六英尺高、燃烧着的黑红字母写着：“为什么？别问为什么。活下去。”

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:58.940
<v Beau O'reilly>And right then, something deep exploded in Eddie. And his face and his heart, his whole being, flushed with joy.
<v Beau O'reilly>就在那一刻，埃迪内心深处爆发了什么。他的脸庞、他的心脏、他的整个人，都充满了喜悦。

00:21:58.940 --> 00:22:23.590
<v Beau O'reilly>Shock treatments are serious and they're undermining. And in Eddie, they led him to a decade of quiet years. Years in which he memorized D.H. Lawrence's Women in Love from cover to cover. But his body, his naked body, lay in waiting. Impatient for the day when the clothes would come off and his body could go public again.
<v Beau O'reilly>休克疗法是严肃的，且具有破坏性。对埃迪来说，这导致了他十年宁静的岁月。在那几年里，他将D.H.劳伦斯的《恋爱中的女人》从头到尾背了下来。但他的身体，他赤裸的身体，一直守候着。不耐烦地等待着那一天：衣服脱掉，他的身体可以再次出现在公众视野中。

00:22:23.590 --> 00:22:34.870
<v Beau O'reilly>Eddie Hickock Collins came to Dekalb, Illinois, to work on the railroad. And he grew a huge, red beard that shouted out a fanfare wherever he went.
<v Beau O'reilly>埃迪·希科克·柯林斯来到伊利诺伊州的迪卡尔布铁路工作。他留起了一部巨大的红胡子，无论走到哪里，那部胡子都在为他进行着狂热的宣传。

00:22:34.870 --> 00:23:01.870
<v Beau O'reilly>The Palace was our vegetarian restaurant theater and coffeehouse. It was work and it was home for we young anti-war hippies. It was a workshop for our ideas on how to change the troubled world that we'd been given by our parents. But it was also a refuge. And a magnet, a magnet for people who were obsessed with one idea. And for the odd.
<v Beau O'reilly>“宫殿”是我们当时素食餐厅的剧院和咖啡馆。那是我们这些年轻反战嬉皮士的工作地和家。那是我们实践那些关于如何改变父母留给我们的这个麻烦世界的想法的实验室。但它也是一个避难所。一个磁铁，一个吸引那些执着于某个理念的人、吸引怪人的磁铁。

00:23:01.870 --> 00:23:28.130
<v Beau O'reilly>If your father was a mason and now you'd lost your chi and you were doomed to wander the five room universe of The Palace looking for it. If you were hopelessly shy and allergic to the 20th century, and everything that made it tick. If you were a closet arsonist who just needed a place to rest and battle the flames inside you. If you were a bottom pincher who drank too much schnapps and read only 17th century literature, you were welcome at The Palace.
<v Beau O'reilly>如果你的父亲是个泥瓦匠，而你现在失去了灵魂，注定要在“宫殿”那五间房的宇宙里徘徊寻找；如果你极其害羞，对一切使20世纪运转的东西过敏；如果你是一个内心渴望纵火但只需要一个地方安顿并与内心火焰战斗的人；如果你是一个整天喝太多杜松子酒、只读17世纪文学的摸底控，那么“宫殿”欢迎你。

