00:25:16.550 --> 00:25:38.220
<v Beau O'reilly>We all laughed not knowing why. And at the end of each performance, we followed Eddie out on the sidewalk. Eddie tossing his clothes in all directions before running off, naked into the night. Dekalb was a small place, but by the next week when Eddie spoke there was a real crowd that followed him outside for his personal unveiling.
<v Beau O'reilly>我们都笑了，却不知道为什么。在每次表演结束时，我们都会跟着埃迪走到人行道上。埃迪将衣服向各个方向抛去，然后赤身裸体地跑进黑夜。迪卡尔布是个小地方，但到了下周埃迪再次演讲时，有一群人真正跟着他走到外面，看他个人的“揭幕仪式”。

00:25:38.220 --> 00:25:53.700
<v Beau O'reilly>Edward Hickock Collins blossomed with nudity and attention. And by the fourth week, with the crowd urging him on, the clothes came off on stage and Eddie became the nude public speaker. Speaking out, but speaking nude, he shouted.
<v Beau O'reilly>爱德华·希科克·柯林斯因裸体和关注而绽放。到了第四周，在人群的怂恿下，衣服在舞台上脱掉了，埃迪成了裸体公开演说家。他大喊着，发言，但他是赤裸着发言。

00:25:53.700 --> 00:26:14.320
<v Beau O'reilly>And Eddie now began his talks naked and he hung around naked. He could be found at The Palace at all hours naked. Sometimes we politely asked him to dress for an occasion like when someone's parents came to town and then Eddie would put on this kilt. A kilt he made out of a pair of cut-off jeans slashed free at the legs.
