00:27:07.120 --> 00:27:29.460
<v Beau O'reilly>And that's the thing about Eddie. As much as he could win you over, and I liked him, he would always find a way to push things just too far. As if any boundary or border was a foreign thing and it was to be disposed of and gotten through, no matter how you felt about it.
<v Beau O'reilly>这就是埃迪的特点。尽管他能赢得你的好感，我也很喜欢他，但他总能找到办法把事情推得太远。就好像任何界限或边界都是外来物，必须被处置和突破，无论你的感受如何。

00:27:29.460 --> 00:27:55.500
<v Beau O'reilly>Eddie moved into our house and invited some of The Palace women to sleep with him. And some of them were happy to do it until the most private details of their intimacy started showing up in his speeches, surrounded by big, blinking exclamation points. Look at this.
<v Beau O'reilly>埃迪搬进我们的房子，邀请了一些“宫殿”的女性和他睡觉。她们中有些人很乐意这样做，直到她们最私密的亲密细节开始出现在他的演讲中，周围环绕着大大的、闪烁的感叹号。你看这个。

00:27:55.500 --> 00:28:22.650
<v Beau O'reilly>The police came two months into Eddie's talks. Eddie was arrested. And soon now, this nude messiah would stand trial. And he felt that, messianic and alone and full of a vision of the world where the pants come down in simultaneous synchronization and whole nations freed from the shackles of clothing, walk freely and hang out in peace.
<v Beau O'reilly>埃迪演讲两个月后，警察来了。埃迪被捕了。现在，这位裸体弥赛亚即将接受审判。他感觉自己像是一个救世主，孑然一身，满怀着对世界的憧憬：在那里，裤子同时落下，整个国家从衣物的枷锁中解放出来，自由行走，在和平中闲逛。

00:28:22.650 --> 00:28:57.050
<v Beau O'reilly>And Eddie spent the weeks prior to his trial alternating phone calls to Brezhnev and the Kremlin and Jimmy Carter's White House. Eddie made his calls from the corner laundry mat, urging long distance operators to support his new strategy. International nudity day July 4. Disarm now. The pants come off in simultaneous synchronization for world peace. That's the hook. If you're naked, how can you take yourself seriously holding a tank or fondling a nuclear war head? You'd have to set them down.
<v Beau O'reilly>埃迪在审判前的几周里，交替着给勃列日涅夫、克里姆林宫和吉米·卡特的白宫打电话。埃迪在街角的洗衣店里打电话，敦促长途接线员支持他的新战略。国际裸体日，7月4日。现在就解除武装。裤子同步落下，以实现世界和平。这就是关键所在。如果你赤身裸体，你怎么能在拿着坦克或抚摸核弹头时还认真对待自己？你不得不放下它们。

00:28:57.050 --> 00:29:13.810
<v Beau O'reilly>Someone at the Kremlin actually answered one of Eddie's calls and Eddie just poured it on over the phone, his whole platform. But at the White House, they just put him on hold and left him there. Eddie hardly noticed. His campaign was heating up.
<v Beau O'reilly>克里姆林宫居然有人接听了埃迪的一个电话，埃迪就在电话里滔滔不绝地讲述他的整个纲领。但在白宫，他们只是让他保持在线，然后就把他晾在那里了。埃迪几乎没注意到。他的竞选正在升温。

00:29:13.810 --> 00:30:23.840
<v Ira Glass>Eddie's trial for indecency and his presidential campaign, which takes him to the 1976 Republican National Convention. That's in a minute, when our program continues.
<v Ira Glass>埃迪因猥亵罪受审以及他的总统竞选活动，将他带到了1976年的共和党全国代表大会。一分钟后，节目继续。

00:30:23.840 --> 00:30:36.460
<v Ira Glass>It's This American Life, I'm Ira Glass. Each week on our program, of course, we choose a theme and bring you a wide variety of stories, different kinds of stories on that theme. Today's show, One Thing. People who are obsessed with one thing.
